  "id": "NPCI-UPI-CHARGES-PRE",
  "title": "UPI: no surcharge; convenience fee disclosed before payment mode",
  "obligation": "The Payee PSP must ensure no surcharge is levied on UPI transactions, and that any convenience fee is disclosed upfront on the merchant payment page before the payment mode is selected. A customer-facing statement about fees must be consistent with that.",
  "source": {
    "regulator": "NPCI",
    "document": "UPI Consolidated Circular Version 1.0",
    "reference": "NPCI/UPI/CC/01",
    "issue_date": "2026-09-18",
    "document_status": "in_force",
    "file": "regulations/irdai-npci-pfrda/NPCI_2026-09-18_upi-consolidated-circular-v1.pdf",
    "sha256": "f238f5afbf025ebc7f0a0a452d7b3937918fc42796d79453fb6ecec36ad05264",
    "text_basis": "native",
    "provenance": "mirror",
    "locator": "para 7.5 as extracted (the PDF text layer interleaves later numbering, so confirm the number against the page)",
    "quotes": [
      "The Payee PSP shall ensure that no surcharge is levied to Users for UPI transactions. In cases where any convenience fees are charged, the Payee PSP shall ensure that such fees are disclosed upfront to the User on the merchant payment page(s) prior to the selection of the payment mode."
    ],
    "url": "third-party mirror; official npci.org.in URL not discoverable (JS-rendered site)"
  },
  "check": {
